<pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.19" change_id="Ia7b4de0f61f7ca8fb337732c54cdbaf5a42bde7d" commit="232d19bfbc65689a0b8649470988752254c7b9ff" commit_message="FROMGIT: Bluetooth: hci_qca: use wait_until_sent() for power pulses  wcn3990 requires a power pulse to turn ON/OFF along with regulators. Sometimes we are observing the power pulses are sent out with some time delay, due to queuing these commands. This is causing synchronization issues with chip, which intern delay the chip setup or may end up with communication issues.  Signed-off-by: Balakrishna Godavarthi &lt;bgodavar@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Marcel Holtmann &lt;marcel@holtmann.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit f9558270b85c865131586fad48d0ecf5b1ea597d git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/bluetooth/bluetooth-next.git master)  BUG=b:111748385 TEST=build for cheza  Change-Id: Ia7b4de0f61f7ca8fb337732c54cdbaf5a42bde7d Signed-off-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1319450 Reviewed-by: Sean Paul &lt;seanpaul@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1319450" owner_email="bgodavar@codeaurora.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/50/1319450/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.19" change_id="Ide68a925bf6c91380bd99d567a6e403282335762" commit="db123d7caa7dce536b844646841be0f2c4b940ef" commit_message="FROMGIT: Bluetooth: hci_qca: Deassert RTS while baudrate change command  This patch will help to stop frame reassembly errors while changing the baudrate. This is because host send a change baudrate request command to the chip with 115200 bps, Whereas chip will change their UART clocks to the enable for new baudrate and sends the response for the change request command with newer baudrate, On host side we are still operating in 115200 bps which results of reading garbage data. Here we are pulling RTS line, so that chip we will wait to send data to host until host change its baudrate.  Signed-off-by: Balakrishna Godavarthi &lt;bgodavar@codeaurora.org&gt; Tested-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Marcel Holtmann &lt;marcel@holtmann.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 78e8fa2972e5583bdda8103925217f5e1215b767  git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/bluetooth/bluetooth-next.git master)  BUG=b:118875972 TEST=on cheza:   no more &quot;Frame reassembly failed&quot; logs during Bluetooth initialization  Change-Id: Ide68a925bf6c91380bd99d567a6e403282335762 Signed-off-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1319451 Reviewed-by: Sean Paul &lt;seanpaul@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1319451" owner_email="bgodavar@codeaurora.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/51/1319451/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.19" change_id="Id51acd13e35c3850c22e978fe0fca36c73c77f11" commit="5f40cadd02a71d7c2945bdb73559346e76481e2f" commit_message="FROMGIT: Bluetooth: hci_qca: Disable IBS state machine and flush Tx buffer  During hci down we observed IBS sleep commands are queued in the Tx buffer and hci_uart_write_work is sending data to the chip which is not required as the chip is powered off. This patch will disable IBS and flush the Tx buffer before we turn off the chip.  Signed-off-by: Balakrishna Godavarthi &lt;bgodavar@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Marcel Holtmann &lt;marcel@holtmann.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 035a960e7a279a59d74585105dcd263559d74f24  git://git.kernel.org/pub/s